        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(feishu): add chunk-idle timeout to inbound media download",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\nFixes an issue where a stalled Feishu (Lark SDK) inbound media download body blocks the channel's agent-reply workflow indefinitely because the underlying Node.js `Readable` async iterator never settles on empty/stalled streams.\n\nAdditionally preserves the existing Feishu timeout policy: the per-chunk idle timeout is now threaded from the caller (`media.ts`) instead of being a hardcoded 30s value hidden inside the helper. Operators with configured timeouts above or below 30s get consistent behavior across connection and body-stall handling.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n- Wrap each `AsyncIterable.next()` call in `Promise.race` against a configurable timeout so stalled Lark SDK bodies cannot hang inbound dispatch.\n- **Do NOT `await` iterator.return()** in the finally block — Node Readable async-iterator `return()` hangs when the underlying source is stalled (waits for a `readable` event that never fires), so awaiting it would block timeout error propagation.\n- Export `FEISHU_INBOUND_MEDIA_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS` (30s), remove the hardcoded default from `saveMediaStreamWithIdleTimeout`, and make `chunkTimeoutMs` a required parameter. Callers (`media.ts`) thread the effective timeout through `saveFeishuResponseMedia`.\n- No new config/env surface. The timeout constant matches Telegram `TELEGRAM_DOWNLOAD_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS = 30_000`.\n\nCollision check: searched open PRs for `media-chunk-idle`, `FeishuInboundMediaTimeoutError`, `withChunkIdleTimeout`, `saveMediaStreamWithIdleTimeout`; no same-file or same-problem open PR was found.\n\n## User Impact\n**Before:** A stalled Feishu media download (e.g., dropped TCP connection after HTTP headers) hangs the agent's inbound processing forever. The hardcoded 30s idle cutoff also ignored operator-configured timeouts.\n\n**After:** Stalled downloads time out after the configured per-chunk idle period (default 30s), the upstream Readable is cleaned up via `iterator.return()`, and the error propagates so downstream dispatch can proceed. Operators with custom timeouts get consistent behavior.\n\n## Verification\n- Exact head: `36b5b89de1c`\n- `oxfmt --check` extensions/feishu/src/media-chunk-idle.ts media.ts media-chunk-idle.test.ts media-chunk-idle.proof.test.ts — All matched files use the correct format.\n- `git diff --check` — passed; exit 0.\n- Focused tests:\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/feishu/src/media-chunk-idle.test.ts -- --run --reporter=verbose\n```\n\n```\n Tests  9 passed (9)\n```\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/feishu/src/media-chunk-idle.proof.test.ts -- --run --reporter=verbose\n```\n\n```\n Tests  3 passed (3)\n```\n\n- Mutation check (previously verified): temporarily restored `await iterator.return()` → test times out at 120s → removed `await` → test passes in ~50ms.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nBehavior addressed: stalled Node.js Readable (Lark SDK boundary) timed out via real `saveMediaStream`; progressing and multi-chunk Readables complete without timeout.\nReal environment tested: Node.js 22.22.0, Linux x86_64, real `saveMediaStream` from `openclaw/plugin-sdk/media-store`, real Node.js `Readable` (same type Lark SDK `getReadableStream()` returns).\n\nProof output (real `saveMediaStream` path):\n\n```\n[feishu media idle production proof] boundary=Readable timed_out=true elapsed_ms=59 chunkTimeoutMs=50\n[feishu media idle production proof] progressing_readable=true size=4 timed_out=false\n[feishu media idle production proof] multi_chunk_readable=true chunks=3 total_bytes=1280 timed_out=false\n```\n\nEvidence:\n- **Stalled Readable times out in ~50ms** (not 120s hang): `new Readable({ read() {} })` → `Promise.race([next(), timeout])` → rejects with `FeishuInboundMediaTimeoutError`.\n- **Progressing Readable completes normally**: `Readable.from([jpeg])` → `result.size=4, contentType=\"image/jpeg\"`.\n- **Multi-chunk Readable**: 3 chunks totaling 1280 bytes, completes within deadline.\n- **Custom timeout below 30s (5s)**: fake timers advance to 5000ms → timeout fires at exactly 5s.\n- **Custom timeout above 30s (60s)**: fake timers advance to 60000ms → timeout fires at exactly 60s.\n- **iterator.return() called exactly once on timeout**: spy confirms cleanup without hanging.\n- **Negative control**: never-yielding `AsyncIterable` without idle wrap stays `still-pending` after 150ms.\n\nWhat was not tested: installed Lark SDK transport with real Feishu tenant (requires Feishu developer account + public webhook). The tested `Readable` type is the exact same Node.js `stream.Readable` that Lark SDK's `getReadableStream()` returns; the idle timeout wrapper operates at the `AsyncIterable` boundary regardless of whether the Readable originates from the SDK or a test.\n\n## Risk / Compatibility\nLow. The `IteratorResult.return()` is fire-and-forget (`.catch(() => undefined)`) so stalled streams never block cleanup. The timeout constant (30s) is the same as Telegram's production idle floor. Timeout is now threaded from the caller so operators with configured Feishu HTTP timeouts can override it. No config, env, or API surface change. Existing media save paths (Buffer, ArrayBuffer, writeFile, Readable) all thread through the same wrapper.\n\nAI-assisted.",
